1. REAL-DATA DIFFERENTIAL (own probe, not the delivered oracle)
   - Copied /home/darrell/bin/ai/budget2/data read-only, twice, into scratch
     (data-master, data-fixed). Wrote a throwaway `_test.go` harness inside
     package `dashboard` (removed after use) that calls
     `dataloader.New→LoadData`, `retirement.NewSettingsManager→Load`,
     `gatherDashboardCalcInputs`, `metrics.Calculate`, and
     `buildBudgetVsActualChartData` exactly as `handleDashboard` does, over
     the full active range (data.MinDate()..MaxDate()).
   - Master tree: `git worktree add --detach <scratch> 040166a`. Fixed tree:
     `cp -a cb-run` with `.git` removed.
   - Both loaded identically: 1275 transactions, target=9700,
     health_target=2255.3, coverage_start=2026-04-28, plan_exclusions_n=0,
     range 2025-02-04..2026-08-27.
   - Result: `metrics_walk` and `chart_walk` are BYTE-IDENTICAL between
     master and fixed (`diff` of the two JSON dumps shows zero difference
     in either array). Independently recomputing net Outflow-type sum per
     calendar month across the full range shows every one of the 19 months
     nets negative (no refund-dominant month exists in this user's live
     ledger today), so zero-diff is the CORRECT prediction, not a null
     result: "points change ONLY in refund-dominant months" holds
     vacuously and honestly (0 refund-dominant months → 0 changed points).
   - Also confirmed real data has 0 `ExcludeFromPlanSync` flags
     (`grep -c ExcludeFromPlanSync major_expenses.json` → 0), so
     monthlyNonExcluded == all Outflow-type transactions for this ledger,
     validating the above per-month net computation as the correct
     real-data proxy for "refund-dominant."

2. SURFACE ENUMERATION (split-classification)
   - `grep -rn CombinedCumulativeBalance|CombinedCumulativeDelta` across
     .go/.html/.js in cb-run: only three arithmetic producers
     (metrics.go, handlers.go's chart walk) and one pass-through consumer
     (kpis.html `data-values="{{toJSON .Metrics.CombinedCumulativeBalance}}"`,
     which serializes the already-computed field, no independent Abs/sign
     logic). `web/static/js/charts.js` only renders a pre-computed values
     array (mode: "balance"); no JS-side recomputation exists.
   - mcpsvc/spend/summary.go exposes CombinedCumulativeDelta (rounded), not
     the per-month walk array — no independent per-month abs arithmetic.
   - Confirmed both fix sites match the manifest exactly
     (`git diff 040166a -- internal/services/metrics/metrics.go` and
     `-- internal/handlers/dashboard/handlers.go`): both change
     `math.Abs(bucket.SumAmount())` → `-bucket.SumAmount()`.
   - MECHANICAL split-classification proof (own mutation, both directions):
     reverting ONLY handlers.go's site (metrics.go fixed) →
     `TestChartCumulativeWalk_AgreesWithMetricsCombinedCumulativeBalance`
     FAILS both subtests (point 0/1 mismatches of ~$4000, i.e. 2x the
     fixture's refund). Reverting ONLY metrics.go's site (handlers.go
     fixed) → the SAME equality test fails AND the new committed regression
     test `TestCalculateMetrics_CombinedCumulativeBalance_
     RefundDominantMonthEntersAsCredit` fails with the exact predicted
     magnitude (Feb step 203.9014 vs wanted 2003.9014, off by 2x900).
     Pristine master (both unfixed): new regression test FAILS (proves the
     defect is real and caught); the chart-equality test PASSES (both
     surfaces share the same bug, so it does NOT gate master — confirms
     the new regression test, not the pre-existing equality test alone, is
     what proves correctness, while the equality test is what proves the
     two surfaces move TOGETHER). This matches the manifest's own
     "Oracle validation record" claim; I re-derived it independently rather
