3. EDGE ATTACKS (own throwaway probes, `probe-fixed` copy, removed after)
   - Refund-dominant FIRST month of an 8-month range, dropped by the
     6-point display cap: tail invariant holds
     (`math.Abs(last-(-delta))<0.01`), and every displayed point differs
     from an otherwise-identical no-refund baseline by EXACTLY the
     predicted constant carry-in (2500.00, i.e. (500 ordinary spend) -
     (-2000 credit)) — proves `running` accumulates before the cap slices
     the display, so a dropped-from-display refund-dominant month still
     propagates correctly into the visible tail.
   - Range that nets refund-dominant OVERALL (wholly refund-dominant
     range): `Calculate` does not panic, produces no NaN — degrades
     honestly, matching the field doc's explicit statement that the
     invariant is "not guaranteed to hold in that case" for this
     documented-out-of-scope precondition.
   - Zero-transaction / exactly-zero bucket: covered by the pre-existing,
     unmodified `_ZeroTransactionMiddleMonth` test (`spend=0.0` when no
     bucket entry exists — sign-agnostic, still passes green).

